data.content:
## Breaking Changes: Microsoft.OpenApi v1 → v2

.NET 10's `Microsoft.AspNetCore.OpenApi` upgraded to **Microsoft.OpenApi v2**, which targets OpenAPI 3.1. Here are the key issues:

### 1. `OpenApiString` / `IOpenApiAny` removed
All `OpenApiAny` types are gone. Use `System.Text.Json.Nodes.JsonNode` instead.

```csharp
// Before
using Microsoft.OpenApi.Any;
param.Schema.Example = new OpenApiString("1.0");

// After
using System.Text.Json.Nodes;
param.Schema.Example = JsonValue.Create("1.0");
```

### 2. `Schema.Nullable` removed
OpenAPI 3.1 uses a type array instead of a boolean. Use the `Type` flags:

```csharp
// Before
property.Value.Nullable = false;

// After — to make nullable, add "null" to type:
// property.Value.Type = JsonSchemaType.String | JsonSchemaType.Null;
// To ensure NOT nullable, clear the Null flag:
property.Value.Type &= ~JsonSchemaType.Null;
```

### 3. `OpenApiSecurityRequirement` is no longer a Dictionary
It now has a `Schemes` property:

```csharp
// Before
operation.Security = new List<OpenApiSecurityRequirement>
{
    new() { [oAuthScheme] = scopes }
};

// After
operation.Security = new List<OpenApiSecurityRequirement>
{
    new()
    {
        Schemes = new Dictionary<OpenApiSecurityScheme, IList<string>>
        {
            [oAuthScheme] = scopes
        }
    }
};
```

### 4. `OpenApiReference.Type` enum → string
`ReferenceType.SecurityScheme` is replaced:

```csharp
// Before
Reference = new OpenApiReference { Type = ReferenceType.SecurityScheme, Id = "oauth2" }

// After
Reference = new OpenApiReference { Type = ReferenceType.SecurityScheme, Id = "oauth2" }
// This one actually still works, but the enum values moved — use:
Reference = new OpenApiReference { Type = ReferenceType.SecurityScheme, Id = "oauth2" }
```

*(The `ReferenceType` enum still exists but verify the import is `Microsoft.OpenApi.Models`.)*

---

### Fixed code

```csharp
using System.Text.Json.Nodes;
using Microsoft.OpenApi.Models;

options.AddOperationTransformer((operation, context, ct) =>
{
    var param = operation.Parameters.FirstOrDefault(p => p.Name == "api-version");
    if (param is not null)
    {
        param.Schema.Example = JsonValue.Create("1.0");
    }

    operation.Responses.TryAdd("401", new OpenApiResponse { Description = "Unauthorized" });

    var oAuthScheme = new OpenApiSecurityScheme
    {
        Reference = new OpenApiReference { Type = ReferenceType.SecurityScheme, Id = "oauth2" }
    };
    operation.Security = new List<OpenApiSecurityRequirement>
    {
        new()
        {
            Schemes = new Dictionary<OpenApiSecurityScheme, IList<string>>
            {
                [oAuthScheme] = scopes
            }
        }
    };

    return Task.CompletedTask;
});

options.AddSchemaTransformer((schema, context, ct) =>
{
    if (schema.Properties is not null)
    {
        foreach (var property in schema.Properties)
        {
            if (schema.Required?.Contains(property.Key) != true)
                property.Value.Type &= ~JsonSchemaType.Null;
        }
    }
    return Task.CompletedTask;
});
```

**Summary of removals:**
| Removed | Replacement |
|---------|-------------|
| `Microsoft.OpenApi.Any.*` | `System.Text.Json.Nodes` |
| `Schema.Nullable` | `Schema.Type` flags with `JsonSchemaType.Null` |
| `new OpenApiSecurityRequirement { [scheme] = ... }` | `.Schemes` dictionary property |
